<title>SINGAPORE: Asian rice prices - April 10.</title>
<headline>Asian rice prices - April 10.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted on Thursday by trading and official sources in the key Asian producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, Pakistan and India in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     April 10  April 3</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 310-350   330-350</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok     670-690   670-690</p>
<p>India-5.0 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB  310	 310</p>
<p>India-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  290	 290</p>
<p>India-15 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  260	 260</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  240	 245</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port     235-245   250-260</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	230-240   240-250</p>
<p>Pakistan-Basmati super FOB Pakistan port	 570-585   580-595</p>
<p>Pakistan-IRRI 6 FOB Pakistan port		  225-230   220-225</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
